+# Literature scan addendum, 2026-10-21 (incremental over LIT_SCAN_2026-10-19.md)
+
+Sources: arXiv export API (ARIS arxiv_fetch.py; abstracts fetched with `id_list=` on 2026-10-21, so every ID below is verified) and WebSearch. No local paper library exists (papers/, literature/). Only papers not in the 2026-10-19 scan are listed.
+
+| Paper | Date | Input → output | What matters for us |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| MIRAGE-CAD, 2608.28669 | 2026-08-24 | text / image / point cloud / STEP → CadQuery-like Python via a construction-plan interface | Build success is only 55–70% and STEP export 52–66%. Execution validity is still the bottleneck for learned generators, which supports making OCC validity primary. |
+| RA-CAD, 2608.05714 | 2026-08-06 | text → CAD code; Generate–Execute–Critique–Rewrite agent | An explicit post-execution critique step before each rewrite. A cheap analogue for our agents: require a one-line critique of the executed-program feedback before the next tool call. |
+| WDR, 2608.04955 | 2026-08-05 | wireframe-stage anomaly detection and repair for generative B-rep | Training-free detect-and-repair before the kernel. Related in spirit to our emit-time revolve check and repair pass, but a different representation. |
+| Pointer-CAD v2, 2606.29301 | 2026-06-28 | plan-then-construct, continuous parameters | Quantization error matters for tolerance. We already emit continuous values. |
+| SOV-CAD, 2607.04119 | 2026-07-05 | images → sequence; stepwise orthographic feedback, offline RL | Stepwise feedback from executed geometry, consistent with tools v2. |
+| VGGT-CAD, 2609.21225 | 2026-09-18 | multi-view images → command sequence | Image input. Low relevance. |
+| ExpConCAD, 2608.24760 | 2026-08-25 | text → CadQuery with experience memory | Low relevance. |
+| GPT-6 Astra CAD case study, 2610.24451 | 2026-10-17 | general model on CAD tasks | Reports a gap between plausible geometry and valid, editable CAD, and says agentic refinement helps only partly. Qualitative. |
+| Extrusion segmentation, 2605.08971 | 2026-05-09 | point cloud → extrusion segments → CAD | Decomposition into extrusions, like our section and loop splitting. |
+
+## Synthesis
+
+No new paper since 2026-10-19 pre-empts the remaining claims. CADFather (2610.09127) is still the closest competitor:
+- It also does execution-aware selection.
+- It counts invalid programs as score 0 and keeps the best valid one ("protected best").
+- It has no repair step and does not use OCC validity checks.
+
+Adoptable ideas, ranked by expected gain on our failure modes:
+1. **A protected valid incumbent from the start** (CADFather's protected best, also the round-1 reviewer's item 6).
+   - On dev4 almost all of the gated gain comes from avoiding zeros. The remaining zeros are no-model outcomes: 00247424 (OOM), and 00730725, 00966713 and 00814797 in some runs.
+   - Fix: execute a cheap valid fallback early and deliver it if the main search fails or is killed.
+2. **Memory limits on candidate subprocesses** so one runaway candidate cannot kill the part (00247424 is OOM in every arm).
+3. **Post-execution critique for agents** (RA-CAD). This is a harness change; evaluate it later under matched budgets.
+4. **SDF-based parameter polishing** (CADFather optimizer). Their own ablation shows only −0.004 to −0.006, so it is low priority.
